Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:44:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] AB monitor 1.6.1: working RAM flush (GUI, headless,
 Windows), native appended .vszh5, exporter 0.1.0, Python 3.12

Monitor 1.6.0 -> 1.6.1
- GUI leak fixed (QTabWidget.clear() never deleted tabs), capped log console,
  worker-thread polling/persistence/flush, only the visible preview rendered.
- One flush path for GUI/headless/caller: persist every output, wait, drop only
  rows every output confirmed (per-row sequence cursors), keep-tail option.
- Flush returns freed memory to the OS: Linux malloc_trim; Windows (1.6.1)
  HeapSetInformation(HeapOptimizeResources) + EmptyWorkingSet, switches
  MEM_RETURN_TO_OS / MEM_TRIM_WORKING_SET, GUI check boxes, commit charge shown.
- 1.6.1 race fix: cursors advance inside the writer task (done-callbacks run
  after result() waiters wake), so a forced persist never resends rows; a
  writer still running is never started twice on one file.
- Trigger gating (minimum interval, minimum store size), process-RSS trigger.
- FITS EXTNAME collision (row multiplication) fixed; atomic FITS/XLSX writes;
  XLSX streamed read-only -> write-only with rollover; CSV/MD append across runs.
- Native .vszh5 appended in place every poll via vszh5_writer 0.0.18
  (LF line endings like the other AB files).
- datetime.utcnow() removed (Python 3.12), duplicate IPs / parameter names,
  ALL_DEVICE_DATA race, call-time HTTP defaults, inf/nan cells.

vszh5_writer 0.0.18: VeuszAppender, resizable VeuszWriter.
Exporter 0.1.0: latest-snapshot model, no stale re-export, real counters.
Caller 1.3.0, examples, stop helper, kit 1.1.0, requirements for 3.12/3.8/3.7.
Tests: meter emulator, offline suites (Linux 3.12/3.8, Windows 3.12 under
Wine), memory-release test, GUI soak. LuaLaTeX manual with bookmarks.

